00:38:36,820 --> 00:38:40,240
And even for long-term space flights, people have to eat.

460
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:49,260
For humans and long-term space missions, it's costing approximately about $10,000 per pound to lift a pound of payload.

461
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:56,080
And if you're going to space, it's very expensive to take soil with you since you want to grow plants.

462
00:38:56,081 --> 00:39:03,360
Today, when the space station food supply is low, a new shipment is sent via an unmanned

463
00:39:03,361 --> 00:39:05,600
spacecraft.

464
00:39:05,601 --> 00:39:09,720
If the craft misses its mark, serious problems can occur.

465
00:39:09,721 --> 00:39:12,400
The hungry crew could be forced to return to Earth.

466
00:39:12,401 --> 00:39:17,960
Or worse, a multi-million dollar mission would have to be aborted.

467
00:39:17,961 --> 00:39:22,560
So plans are underway to grow enough food for the space station to be self-sufficient.

468
00:39:22,561 --> 00:39:34,100
The Tuskegee scientists began their work with two of George Washington Carver's favorite plants.

469
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:36,480
The peanut.

470
00:39:38,300 --> 00:39:39,460
And the sweet potato.

471
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:44,660
Our job was to take Carver's two commodities, he was most famous for,

472
00:39:44,740 --> 00:39:47,020
and figure out how to grow them, first of all, with no soil.

473
00:39:47,400 --> 00:39:48,460
That was our first job.

474
00:39:49,100 --> 00:39:51,160
Now, isn't that a setup for Carver?

475
00:39:51,161 --> 00:39:54,320
I mean, wouldn't that be right down his alley?

476
00:39:55,560 --> 00:40:01,820
The Department of Agricultural Sciences at Tuskegee pursued a unique hydroponics-based growing system

477
00:40:01,821 --> 00:40:04,020
called nutrient film technique.

478
00:40:04,980 --> 00:40:10,420
It requires no soil and relies only on water and a mixture of growing agents.

479
00:40:11,740 --> 00:40:18,380
And the nutrient solution flows continuously over the roots as the plants grow.

480
00:40:18,381 --> 00:40:24,380
The tiny roots form a fibrous carpet, or soil-less bed, for the plants.

481
00:40:24,381 --> 00:40:29,380
After two or three weeks, the potato starts to change color and bulk up.

482
00:40:31,380 --> 00:40:39,380
As part of the NASA program, the university also built growth chambers to produce basil and carrots in the same way.

483
00:40:39,381 --> 00:40:44,380
We can control how much light they get, what time they get it, the temperature.

484
00:40:44,381 --> 00:40:52,140
and not only just one temperature we can actually ramp the temperature up just like nature does it

485
00:40:53,380 --> 00:40:59,140
the Tuskegee scientists tested their growing system for several years when they were sure

486
00:40:59,141 --> 00:41:04,120
that it would work in a space environment they shared their findings with NASA and when the NASA

487
00:41:04,121 --> 00:41:12,320
folks came from Kennedy Space Center to see it they could not believe it but there was so that's

488
00:41:12,321 --> 00:41:15,980
That's why I'm saying it took some really, I would say Carverites are brilliant young

489
00:41:15,981 --> 00:41:19,560
faculty and students who just stayed at it.

490
00:41:19,561 --> 00:41:26,760
Today, a new crop of Carvers in training is sprouting up in San Antonio, Texas.

491
00:41:26,761 --> 00:41:31,180
If it would have had real shallow roots, way up here and that's it, do you think it'd

492
00:41:31,181 --> 00:41:33,360
be able to tap way down and get some water?

493
00:41:33,361 --> 00:41:38,300
The Carver Academy is dedicated to keeping the spirit of George Washington Carver fresh

494
00:41:38,301 --> 00:41:40,760
in the minds of today's youth.

495
00:41:40,761 --> 00:41:45,620
The school was founded by former NBA superstar David Robinson.

496
00:41:46,960 --> 00:41:54,520
It started more because I grew up kind of with a teacher's heart and always wanted to teach, always loved teaching.

497
00:41:55,520 --> 00:41:59,480
And since I became a basketball player, teaching was pretty much out of the question.

498
00:41:59,740 --> 00:42:03,220
But I've always loved inspiring and stirring the heart.

499
00:42:04,540 --> 00:42:09,620
The school emphasizes the same hands-on learning techniques that Carver practiced in his career.

500
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:16,760
And the teachers also try to instill in the children a curiosity about the world around them.

501
00:42:16,761 --> 00:42:19,760
They may like have those lights in there.

502
00:42:19,761 --> 00:42:23,760
You know, nature speaks to us every hour. If you would just listen.

503
00:42:23,761 --> 00:42:24,830
We're so tech-oriented.

504
00:42:24,831 --> 00:42:29,760
We know everybody wants to play with the latest gadgets and see what, you know, science is coming up with.

505
00:42:29,761 --> 00:42:33,012
Well, the most incredible things we have are right there in nature.

506
00:42:33,013 --> 00:42:34,760
They're right in front of our faces.

507
00:42:34,761 --> 00:42:37,760
They're the plants that grow right in front of us.

508
00:42:37,761 --> 00:42:43,040
And the kids have access to the most remarkable resources every single day.

509
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:44,160
It's overflowing.

510
00:42:45,900 --> 00:42:49,360
The Carver Academy is perhaps the best tribute to the scientist

511
00:42:49,361 --> 00:42:51,700
who was constantly honored during his lifetime.

512
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:56,440
He accepted every award with his signature humility.

513
00:42:58,040 --> 00:43:03,760
I am not sure that I am worthy of this splendid citation.

514
00:43:03,761 --> 00:43:10,600
but I wish to say also that I thank you from the depth of my heart.

515
00:43:11,080 --> 00:43:15,080
He just refused to give himself credit when he did.

516
00:43:15,600 --> 00:43:17,800
He gives the credit to God.

517
00:43:19,620 --> 00:43:24,280
On January 5th, 1943, at the age of 78,

518
00:43:25,740 --> 00:43:29,240
Carver died of natural causes in his room at Tuskegee Institute.

519
00:43:29,241 --> 00:43:38,740
Six months later, President Franklin Roosevelt established the George Washington Carver National

520
00:43:38,741 --> 00:43:43,160
